# Agent handoff — use `_DEPLOY_QUEUE.md`

All Machine-1 sessions share one working copy. **Do not commit, push, or deploy** unless you are repo owner **#1**. See `commit-deploy-policy.mdc`.

## When your work is ready

Append **one line** to `_DEPLOY_QUEUE.md` (Queue section):

```text
[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] #<n> <session name> — <files changed> — <staging|production> — <one-line description> — STATUS: pending
```

Example:

```text
[2026-06-28 14:00] #CW Invoice redesign — cch-invoice-redesign.js, cch-proposals-invoices-fix.js, index.html — staging — Client View on main page — STATUS: pending
```

- Default target: **staging** unless Cindy gave explicit production GO.
- Do **not** message Cindy for deploy — queue it; #1 batches hourly.

## Handoff block (for Docs or chat summary)

When writing a handoff doc or ending a substantive session, include:

1. **Changed files** — path + one-line what changed
2. **Deploy target** — staging / production / functions-only
3. **Pre-deploy checks** — `node --check` files, cache buster bumps
4. **Verify steps** — URL, hard refresh, specific page/doc to open
5. **Guardrails** — isolation, no prod deploy, staging doc IDs if relevant
6. **STATUS** — `pending` until #1 deploys

## #1 (Deploy Master) checklist

1. Read `_DEPLOY_QUEUE.md` pending lines
2. Batch related staging items (one deploy at a time for readability)
3. Run pre-deploy checks from handoff
4. Deploy staging first; production only on Cindy GO
5. Flip line to `STATUS: done (staging deploy YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM)` or prod equivalent

## Session logs

Substantive sessions: `Docs/SESSION_LOG_Cursor_YYYY-MM-DD.md` per `nightly-session-log.mdc`.
